#[=======================================================================[.rst:
RBLXBuildForceCompiler
------------------

.. deprecated:: 3.6

  Do not use.

  The commands provided by this module were once intended for use by
  cross-compiling toolchain files when RBLXBuild was not able to automatically
  detect the compiler identification.  Since the introduction of this module,
  RBLXBuild's compiler identification capabilities have improved and can now be
  taught to recognize any compiler.  Furthermore, the suite of information
  RBLXBuild detects from a compiler is now too extensive to be provided by
  toolchain files using these macros.

  One common use case for this module was to skip RBLXBuild's checks for a
  working compiler when using a cross-compiler that cannot link binaries
  without special flags or custom linker scripts.  This case is now supported
  by setting the :variable:`RBLXBUILD_TRY_COMPILE_TARGET_TYPE` variable in the
  toolchain file instead.

Load this module in a RBLXBuild toolchain file:

.. code-block:: rblxbuild

  include(RBLXBuildForceCompiler)

Commands
^^^^^^^^

This module provides the following commands:

.. command:: rblxbuild_force_c_compiler

  Sets the :variable:`RBLXBUILD_C_COMPILER <RBLXBUILD_<LANG>_COMPILER>` variable to
  the given compiler and the :variable:`RBLXBUILD_C_COMPILER_ID
  <RBLXBUILD_<LANG>_COMPILER_ID>` variable to the given compiler-id:

  .. code-block:: rblxbuild

    rblxbuild_force_c_compiler(<compiler> <compiler-id>)

  This command also bypasses the check for working compiler and basic
  compiler information tests.

.. command:: rblxbuild_force_cxx_compiler

  Sets the :variable:`RBLXBUILD_CXX_COMPILER <RBLXBUILD_<LANG>_COMPILER>` variable
  to the given compiler and the :variable:`RBLXBUILD_CXX_COMPILER_ID
  <RBLXBUILD_<LANG>_COMPILER_ID>` variable to the given compiler-id:

  .. code-block:: rblxbuild

    rblxbuild_force_cxx_compiler(<compiler> <compiler-id>)

  This command also bypasses the check for working compiler and basic
  compiler information tests.

.. command:: rblxbuild_force_fortran_compiler

  Sets the :variable:`RBLXBUILD_Fortran_COMPILER <RBLXBUILD_<LANG>_COMPILER>`
  variable to the given compiler and the
  :variable:`RBLXBUILD_Fortran_COMPILER_ID <RBLXBUILD_<LANG>_COMPILER_ID>` variable
  to the given compiler-id:

  .. code-block:: rblxbuild

    rblxbuild_force_fortran_compiler(<compiler> <compiler-id>)

  This command also bypasses the check for working compiler and basic
  compiler information tests.

Examples
^^^^^^^^

A simple toolchain file using this module could look like this:

.. code-block:: rblxbuild
  :caption: ``rblxbuild/toolchains/example-toolchain.rblxbuild``

  include(RBLXBuildForceCompiler)
  set(RBLXBUILD_SYSTEM_NAME Generic)
  rblxbuild_force_c_compiler(chc12 MetrowerksHicross)
  rblxbuild_force_cxx_compiler(chc12 MetrowerksHicross)

In new RBLXBuild code, compiler is detected automatically when setting required
variables instead:

.. code-block:: rblxbuild
  :caption: ``rblxbuild/toolchains/example-toolchain.rblxbuild``

  set(RBLXBUILD_SYSTEM_NAME Generic)
  set(RBLXBUILD_C_COMPILER chc12)
  set(RBLXBUILD_CXX_COMPILER chc12)

See Also
^^^^^^^^

* :manual:`rblxbuild-toolchains(7)`
#]=======================================================================]

macro(RBLXBUILD_FORCE_C_COMPILER compiler id)
  message(DEPRECATION "The RBLXBUILD_FORCE_C_COMPILER macro is deprecated.  "
    "Instead just set RBLXBUILD_C_COMPILER and allow RBLXBuild to identify the compiler.")
  set(RBLXBUILD_C_COMPILER "${compiler}")
  set(RBLXBUILD_C_COMPILER_ID_RUN TRUE)
  set(RBLXBUILD_C_COMPILER_ID ${id})
  set(RBLXBUILD_C_COMPILER_FORCED TRUE)

  # Set old compiler id variables.
  if(RBLXBUILD_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "GNU")
    set(RBLXBUILD_COMPILER_IS_GNUCC 1)
  endif()
endmacro()

macro(RBLXBUILD_FORCE_CXX_COMPILER compiler id)
  message(DEPRECATION "The RBLXBUILD_FORCE_CXX_COMPILER macro is deprecated.  "
    "Instead just set RBLXBUILD_CXX_COMPILER and allow RBLXBuild to identify the compiler.")
  set(RBLXBUILD_CXX_COMPILER "${compiler}")
  set(RBLXBUILD_CXX_COMPILER_ID_RUN TRUE)
  set(RBLXBUILD_CXX_COMPILER_ID ${id})
  set(RBLXBUILD_CXX_COMPILER_FORCED TRUE)

  # Set old compiler id variables.
  if("${RBLXBUILD_CXX_COMPILER_ID}" MATCHES "GNU")
    set(RBLXBUILD_COMPILER_IS_GNUCXX 1)
  endif()
endmacro()

macro(RBLXBUILD_FORCE_Fortran_COMPILER compiler id)
  message(DEPRECATION "The RBLXBUILD_FORCE_Fortran_COMPILER macro is deprecated.  "
    "Instead just set RBLXBUILD_Fortran_COMPILER and allow RBLXBuild to identify the compiler.")
  set(RBLXBUILD_Fortran_COMPILER "${compiler}")
  set(RBLXBUILD_Fortran_COMPILER_ID_RUN TRUE)
  set(RBLXBUILD_Fortran_COMPILER_ID ${id})
  set(RBLXBUILD_Fortran_COMPILER_FORCED TRUE)

  # Set old compiler id variables.
  if(RBLXBUILD_Fortran_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "GNU")
    set(RBLXBUILD_COMPILER_IS_GNUG77 1)
  endif()
endmacro()
